{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 132, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a skip with a 3x3 conv gave large gains in the skip-heavy parents (runs 53, 55), while replacing other ops gave small or mixed changes."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling edge with a conv helps a lot when the cell has few convs (run 54)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping the final skip for a 3x3 conv gave consistent gains (runs 83, 85, 88), larger than when replacing a conv or none edge."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing the pooling edge with a conv improved all three datasets (runs 81, 84, 86), more than replacing a 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 1 means the cell has few convs, so adding a conv on edge 0 yields a large gain (runs 13, 15)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "With a skip on edge 5 the cell lacks convolutions, so a conv on edge 4 adds much more (runs 3, 5) than in conv-rich parents (run 7)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Turning edge 0 into a skip when edge 1 is already a skip removes the remaining convolutional capacity, giving a large drop (runs 73, 75)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 3 marks a conv-poor cell, so a 3x3 conv on edge 5 helps more (runs 83, 90)."}, {